  "raw_text": "82\n\nKakahbra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \none who arranges, one who imposes, one who\n \nsets, one who places, one who\n\naims\n \n/\n \nuno\n \nque arregla,\n \nuno\n \nque impone,\n \nuno\n \nque establece,\n \nuno\n \nque coloca,\n \nuno\n \nque apunta\n\nKapka kakahbra\n \n(\nmy83\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ncupbearer\n \n/ copero\n\nLalma kahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto dawn, to begin to show light in the morning\n \n/ amanecer, alborear, comenzar a mostrar luz\npor la mañana\n\nUn kahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto answer, to heed\n \n/ responder, contestar\n\n(Construct:\n \nUni kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto answer me\n \n/ respondeme;\n \nUnam kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto answer you\n \n/ responderte;\n \nAi una\n \n–\n \nto answer\nhim/her/it\n \n/ responderle)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 50:2\n):\n \nYang bal winri bara dîa muni upla kum sin uni kahbras kan ba?\n \n–\n \nWhy did no one answer me when\nI called?\n \n/ ¿Por qué nadie me respondió cuando llamé?)\n\nYula kahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto accompany, to go along with\n \n/ acompañar, ir con\n\n(Construct:\n \nYuli kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto go along with me\n \n/ acompañarme;\n \nYulam kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto go along with you\n \n/ acompañarte)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-09/20\n):\n \nJisas ba ai yula kahbi kan mairka nani ra kulki kan ba nahki marikan?\n \n–\n \nHow did Jesus show he valued\nthe women accompanying him?\n \n/ ¿Cómo demostró Jesús que valoraba a las mujeres que lo acompañaban?\n)\n\nYula kahbi uplika\n \n(a/t:\n \nYula kahbi ba\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npartner, the person going along with\n \n/ pareja, la persona\nque acompaña\n\nYula kakahbra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \npartner, person going along with\n \n/ pareja, persona que acompaña\n\n(Construct:\n \nYuli kakahbra\n;\n \nYulam kakahbra\n)\n\nKahmi\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncalabash, bottle-gourd, gourd, bowl, bowl made from the calabash\n \n/ jícaro, guacal, jícara, cuenco hecho\nde jícaro\n\nKahmi dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncalabash tree\n \n/ árbol de\n \njícaro\n\nKahra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npole, long stick, pole used to determine depth of water\n \n/ palo, palanca, palo utilizado para medir la\n\nprofundidad del agua\n\nKahwa\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSkahwa\n\nKahwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get stuck, to stall, to run aground\n \n/ atascarse, encallar\n\n(Note/Nota: There are a few places where\n \nKahwan\n \n(v-3p-past of: Kahwaia) is used to say\n \nfell\n \nbut\n \nKauhan\n \n(v-3p-past of: Kauhaia)\nseems to be correct / Hay algunos lugares donde se usa\n \nKahwan\n \n(v-3p-pasado de: Kahwaia) para decir\n \ncayó\n, pero Kauhan (v-3p-\npasado de: Kauhaia) parece ser correcto)\n\nKaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be\n \n/ ser, estar\n\nBan kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be forever, to live forever, to continue to be, to always be\n \n/ ser para siempre, vivir para siempre,\nseguir siendo, ser siempre\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nAisa yapti nani dîa daukaia sip sa ai luhpia nani ban tânka kasak ra kaia hilp munaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat\ncan parents do in order to help their children to continue to be in the truth?\n \n/ ¿Qué pueden hacer los padres para ayudar a\nsus hijos a seguir en la verdad?)\n\nBan kaia ra\n \n–\n \nfor forever, for always\n \n/ para siempre, eternamente\n\nB\nan kaia\n \nra\n \niwaia\n \n(v\n)\n \n–\n \nto live forever\n \n/ vivir para siempre\n\nBan kaia Kingka\n \n(\n1Timoti 1:17\n)\n \n–\n \nKing of Eternity\n \n/ Rey de la eternidad\n\nRaya ban kaia\n \n(v\n)\n \n–\n \nto be alive forever\n \n/ estar vivo para siempre\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \neverlasting life\n \n/ vida eterna\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka briaia b\nî\nla kaikanka ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe hope of everlasting life\n \n/ la\n\nesperanza de la vida eterna\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka yabalka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroad to everlasting\n \nlife\n \n/ camino a la vida eterna\n\nBas\n \n(v\n-\nimp\n \nof\n/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nbe\n \n/\n \ns\né\n, sea, sean\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nKarna bas\n \n–\n \nbe strong\n \n/ sé fuerte\n)\n\nKaia kan\n \n–\n \nwas to be, were to be\n \n/ debía ser\n\nKaia sa\n \n–\n \nmust be, is to be, must, must be the case, must be true, must be the situation\n \n/ debe ser/estar, debe,\ndebe ser el caso, debe ser cierto, debe ser la situación\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh29\n):\n \nSetan wali kan kaia sa\n \n–\n \nIt must be that Satan was listening\n \n/ Debe ser que Satanás estaba escuchando)\n\nKabia\n \n(v-3p-fut II of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwill be\n \n/ estarán\n\nKabia kra\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nmight be, might become\n \n/ podría ser, podría convertirse\n\nKaisa\n \n(v-3p-fut I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwill be, let’s, let’s be, let’s be do\ning this\n \n/ será, seamos, vamos, vamos a hacer,\nhagamos esto\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKapu,Kap\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKaisa baiki sakanka 5 ba aisi kaikaia\n \n–\n \nLet’s read paragraph 5\n \n/ Leamos el párrafo 5)",
